The demon would be unusual at very shallow depths. The only kinds of
demon that will be randomly generated at these kind of depths are
water demon, succubus and incubus.

HOWEVER - there is a monster called a "chameleon", which can appear
like literally ANY monster in the game - and has the powers of that
monster. It changes appearance every few turns. If you're wearing a
ring of protection from shape changers, it appears as a pretty weak
":" (i.e. lizard-type) monster with nothing but a very weak bite
attack.

My best guess is:
 - you stepped on a "magic trap". This can have any of a number of
effects:
exploding (gives you extra Power points),
erupting in a tower of flame (fire damage),
summoning monsters all around you,
taming monsters right next to you and giving you a point of charisma,
casting remove curse on you,
or a variety of different "special effects" that are just there for
flavour.

This particular one decided, on this particular occasion, to summon
monsters, rather than do any of the other possible effects. Hardly
surprising, as this seems to be one of the more common random effects
from this type of trap. Oh... and it also blinds you with a flash of
light when it does this: but if you have the power of Telepathy (for
instance, after having eaten a floating eye corpse, which always gives
you this power intrinsically) you will still be able to see any
monsters that have a mind.

 - and the monsters included a chameleon, who appeared in the form of
a red "&" and had the powers of that monster for a short while. If
you'd survived for another few turns it would have turned into
something else, which could have been as weak as a lichen or as strong
as an arch-lich...

...and in fact the killer bees were more likely to kill you than the
"demon" which wasn't a real demon, although it looked like one for a
few turns and had the powers of one for a few turns.

